mptcp-bpf-weight (1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split the bpf_weight_rr scheduler out into its own mptcp-bpf-weight-rr
    source package (see that package's debian/ directory) so it can be
    installed/versioned independently of bpf_weight. mptcp-weight-manager
    stays here and still manages either scheduler's weights, since both
    share the same endpoint_weights/weight_remote_id BPF maps.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

mptcp-bpf-weight (1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of the bpf_weight and bpf_weight_rr MPTCP
    schedulers and their shared mptcp-scheduler-weight.sh manager, for
    the server/VPS side of an OpenMPTCProuter multipath link. Adds the
    weight_remote_id weighting mode (MPTCP remote endpoint id -> weight)
    needed there, since every subflow on the VPS shares the same local
    IP and can't be distinguished by endpoint_weights' local-IP keying
    alone -- mirrors mptcp-bpf-dscp's dscp_iface/dscp_remote_id split.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
